      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "The seven continents are <b>Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, North America and South America</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "why",
        "html": "A continent is a huge area of land that holds many countries (Antarctica has none). Some places count the continents a little differently, for example by joining North and South America into one. In the United States, most schools count seven."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Country or continent?",
        "q": "Is Africa a country?",
        "steps": [
          "Africa is one of the seven continents.",
          "It holds many countries: 54 that are members of the United Nations."
        ],
        "a": "No. Africa is a continent with more than 50 countries."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "gg-sort",
        "opts": {
          "bins": [
            "Continent",
            "Not a continent"
          ],
          "cards": [
